## Auction lots that may *look* like “Stradivarius” but need expert authentication

- **Hawleys Auctioneers — lot text referencing “Antonius Stradivarius Cremonensis Faciebat Anno 1725” labeling (May–June 2025 sale)**  
  - https://www.hawleys.info/catalogue/lot/7ed57fb194dd4d0f3cc4e51e3ee9ca97/930676c09557b5f2fb9f2ea106674265/may-antiques-fine-art-2025-lot-1276/  
  - **Note:** trade reporting on similarly described small-auction lots often indicates a **facsimile label / composite instrument**, not a multi-million-pound Stradivari. Always read condition reports and certificates.

---

## Practical next step if you intend to purchase an authentic Stradivari

1. Engage an independent violin expert / restorer for condition and attribution.  
2. Request **photography, dendrochronology where applicable, and full certificate chain** (Hill, Beare, etc.).  
3. Register as a bidder or negotiate private treaty through a recognized dealer.  

---

## Disclaimer

URLs can move, lots can be withdrawn, and search indexes lag reality. This document is **not** investment or authentication advice.
